meta {
  name: Overage - Update
  type: http
  seq: 18
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/billing/overage
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "enabled": true,
    "limit": 50000
  }
}

docs {
  Turns credit overage on or off and sets its cap. Requires the
  `billing.manage` permission.

  - `enabled` — required boolean. Enabling on a plan without the
    `credit_overage` feature 403s with `FeatureNotAvailableException` rather
    than saving a setting that would do nothing.
  - `limit` — optional. Overage credits this workspace may accrue per billing
    period. May be lowered but never raised above `maximum_limit` (a 422),
    so overage can't run away unbounded. Send `null` to clear the choice and
    fall back to the estate default. Omit the key to leave it unchanged.

  Overage credits are billed after the fact at `credit_value_usd` each by
  `billing:invoice-overage`, not at the moment they are spent.

  Response is wrapped: `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { overage } }`,
  the same shape `Overage - Get` returns.
}
